{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 53, :comments ["<b>And you shall dispossess the land and dwell in it, for to you I have given the land to possess it</b> — In my opinion this is a positive commandment. He commands them to dwell in the land and to possess it, for He has given it to them, and they must not despise the heritage of YHWH. And if it were to arise in their minds to go and conquer the land of Shinar or the land of Assyria or elsewhere and to settle there, they would transgress the commandment of YHWH. And that which our Sages (Ketubot 110b) emphasized concerning the commandment of dwelling in the Land of Israel, and that it is forbidden to leave it, and they ruled that she is like a rebelling wife who does not wish to go up with her husband to the Land of Israel, and likewise the man — it is here that we are commanded in this commandment, for this verse is a positive commandment. And this commandment recurs in many places: \"Come and possess the land\" (Deuteronomy 1:8). But Rashi explained (Rashi on Numbers 33:53): \"And you shall dispossess the land\" — and you shall dispossess it of its inhabitants, then \"and you shall dwell in it\" — you will be able to endure in it, and if not, you will not be able to endure in it. But what we have explained is the principal meaning."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:10:13.772881884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}